# postfix FHS migration: remove the stray /run/postfix runtime dir.
#
# Split-brain resolved, not moved: the OpenRC initd tracked a flat
# pidfile at /run/postfix-master.pid and created an otherwise
# unconsumed /run/postfix directory, while the systemd unit and
# postfix itself always used the queue-native
# /var/spool/postfix/pid/master.pid. The fix aligns the initd to the
# queue-native path (initd pidfile corrected alongside); there is no
# /var/run path for postfix at all - queue state lives under
# /var/spool/postfix (accounts.d dir stanza, persistent).
#
# Stale-state policy: the master validates pid liveness itself
# (live duplicate refused, stale reclaimed); `postfix check`
# validates queue structure at every start in both inits.
# Old residue is the empty-or-absent /run/postfix dir plus the flat
# /run/postfix-master.pid file, both on tmpfs: the dir is removed
# once empty, the pidfile needs no migration (reboot-cleared,
# unread post-move).

rmdir-if-empty /run/postfix
